s=json.loads((R/'summary.json').read_text());lines=['# Fixed-v3 host ground occlusion / primary emission','', 'Status: NOT_ESTABLISHED, not adopted. This is a host-only transport experiment, not firmware/Pocket integration or a device performance result. Original scene, all fixed reference conditions, domain masks and thresholds remain unchanged.','', '## Contract and controls','Three arms use identical existing pixel DISK16 + one diffuse bounce outer16/inner16. OFF omits the floor. CONTROL adds only the source finite opaque floor to direct and transport rays. LE adds only primary-hemisphere first-floor-hit rhoX×Le. World misses and floor hits are exclusive; no floor BSDF reflection, secondary floor emission, camera/background floor, AgX, weighted filter, specular or higher bounce is introduced. Thus opaque-black-floor CONTROL is deliberately a component ablation, not a complete physical rendering of the authored ground.','', 'All 60 actual C frames completed under unchanged quotas. OFF all 40 RGB/depth buffers are exact against prior bounce-001. Each arm has exact final forward/reverse colors and depth, and all depth matches the old candidate. These are pixel invariants, not a claim of equal intermediate work/order timing. Input hashes remained unchanged.','', 'Source ground geometry/material was independently read, copied and owned; RGB emission is already linear, strength .25, with no sRGB decode. Auxiliary Blender front/back emission agrees with source Le within 5.96e-8. This fixture was artifact/source audited independently, not independently re-rendered. Floor geometry affects rays only, so reference silhouette omissions and missing background support remain.','', '## Fixed-domain results','Full metrics, false positives/negatives, pooled/uncertain values and condition masks are in the score folders and metrics.json. Unknown regions never become a PASS. Values below are stable-domain diagnostics; no single average establishes the 60% goal.','']
