d=[s['le'][k]['RGB']-s['control'][k]['RGB'] for k in s['le']];lines += [f"LE versus CONTROL recovers {min(d):.4f} to {max(d):.4f} RGB points in every condition, but does not recover the floor-omitted baseline. This identifies a source-derived contribution without claiming overall improvement.", '', '## Source-radiance interpretation', 'At baseline the original uniform world radiance is (.35,.308,.2415), whereas source floor Le is (.21,.195,.1625). Replacing previously unoccluded downward world misses by floor Le therefore reduces that direct radiance, before any reference comparison. Floor BSDF reflection and secondary emission are deliberately absent, so this is not a complete floor-transport solution and does not prove the authored floor makes the original image darker.', '', '## Numerical limits', 'The finite-square known fixture has exact cosine fraction .554126424, independent Cartesian512² .554126981. Actual outer16=.5 (−9.77%), outer64=.5625 (+1.51%); dense cosine16384=.554199219. These are one fixture’s errors, not whole-character error bounds. No sample count, light gain, source color or threshold is fitted to pictures. Prior 64-sample budget failure is preserved. Fine tests below are separate, not substituted into the main score.']
f=R/'fine-002/results.json'
if f.exists():
 for x in json.loads(f.read_text())['records']:lines += [f"- Fine oblique {x['case']}: {x['status']}; return code {x['returncode']}; stderr {x['stderr'].strip()!r}."]
lines += ['', 'The first fine helper attempt failed before rendering because its generated ground input path omitted inputs/. It is preserved as fine-001.log; fine-002 uses the pinned scenario input path. This is not a renderer/quota failure.', '', '## Ownership, budgets and costs', 'Snapshot65536B/work8M remain unchanged; snapshot actual52212B/45records, model arena65892B, cold35636B, instance584B. Direct budgets1M rays/100M nodes/50M triangles; transport20M/800M/300M are separate frame-cumulative quotas. Render failure leaves incomplete bands unpublished; partial artifacts are never scored.', 'Owned BVH OFF326496B/ON327056B. Owned transport OFF75184B/ON75312B. ON sum402368B per generation; two retained generations804736B, excluding allocator overhead, two snapshots and scratch. The two-generation concurrency policy is caller-managed, not globally enforced. Ground increases even OFF transport header by56B; render context272B versus184B old. Input geometry temporary34368→34488B, attributes74624→74752B. Geometry/pose/light/material/emission generations are caller-issued and bound to exact copied inputs, not automatic persistent scene-change detection.', 'Actual all-case budgets and reverse-order work counters are retained in accounting and native metadata. No new large observer framebuffer is used. These host memory costs are not a claim that the device fits. F64/FPU device timing is unknown.']
t=R/'timing-001/results.json'
if t.exists():
 j=json.loads(t.read_text());lines += ['', 'Controlled unsanitized O2 host CPU: three alternating repetitions per arm/all ten forward cases; reverse functional-run costs are separately retained, not compared as controlled timings.']
